# Finalize character and vehicle assets, animations, and equivalence

Finalize content assets after the game is already behaviorally complete and
playable. At this stage each converted asset has a known Unreal consumer and a
known gameplay contract, so equivalence can be tested against real usage.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Finalize all character and vehicle geometry, skeletons, physics assets,
  animations, materials, attachments, and presentation behavior.
- [ ] Finish remaining native asset conversion and retire transitional FBX
  consumers only where native parity is proven.
- [ ] Run representative and corpus-wide equivalence tests against actual
  gameplay consumers rather than editor appearance alone.
- [ ] Do not change authored transforms or scales to compensate for a runtime or
  consumer defect.

## Dependencies

Depends on the functionally complete missions, menus, roster, and progression
phase.
